  <h1>IVD Kit Storage &amp; Transport</h1>

  <p><strong>Direct answer:</strong> Colloidal-gold rapid tests are room-temperature stable and need no cold chain — keep them sealed with desiccant until use.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Requirement</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Temperature</th><td>Room temperature (typically 2–30 °C)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Moisture</th><td>Keep in sealed pouch with desiccant until use</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Light</th><td>Protect from direct sunlight</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Cold chain</th><td>Not required (colloidal-gold lateral flow)</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Shelf life</th><td>Typically 24 months (product-specific)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>
    Colloidal-gold lateral-flow tests are room-temperature stable — a key advantage for tropical and
    remote distribution. Exact dating is per product/configuration. See the
    <a href="/rfq/">RFQ</a> page to request stability data.
  </p>

  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <p><strong>Do colloidal-gold rapid tests need a cold chain?</strong> No — they are room-temperature stable when kept sealed with desiccant.</p>
  </div>

